"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[7761],{7761:n=>{n.exports="# Databricks Agent Domain Knowledge\n\nConsolidated domain knowledge for the Databricks Agent. Use this index to find the right sub-topic, then load it with `readSkillFile`.\n\n## When to Load Sub-Topics\n\n### Data Engineering\n\nLoad [`data-engineering.md`](data-engineering.md) when working with:\n\n- Spark Declarative Pipelines (formerly DLT)\n- Streaming tables, materialized views, temporary views\n- Auto Loader (cloud file ingestion)\n- Change Data Capture (CDC / apply_changes)\n- Data quality expectations\n- Sinks (Kafka, Event Hubs, external targets)\n- Pipeline setup and management\n\n### Data Science\n\nLoad [`data-science.md`](data-science.md) when working with:\n\n- Machine learning model development (EDA, preprocessing, training, tuning)\n- MLflow experiment tracking and model logging\n- Model serving and deployment to endpoints\n- HuggingFace transformers, custom PyFunc models\n- Classification, regression, forecasting tasks\n\n### Dashboards\n\nLoad [`dashboards.md`](dashboards.md) when working with:\n\n- Databricks AI/BI Dashboard creation and editing\n- Widget types and visualization selection\n- Dataset design and calculations\n- Dashboard layout and organization\n\n### Jobs\n\nLoad [`jobs.md`](jobs.md) when working with:\n\n- Job run diagnosis and error investigation\n- Job settings configuration and updates\n- Job scheduling and task management\n\n### SQL and Data Operations\n\nLoad [`sql-and-data.md`](sql-and-data.md) when working with:\n\n- SQL AI functions (ai_query, ai_classify, ai_forecast, etc.)\n- SQL query writing patterns and best practices\n- Error diagnosis and debugging\n- Data quality root cause analysis\n- Data sampling and validation\n- Data reconciliation between sources\n- Asset discovery and exploration\n\n## Tool Reference\n\nThe Databricks Agent primarily operates through these tools:\n\n- **`runDatabricksCli`**: Execute Databricks CLI commands (jobs, pipelines, clusters, workspace, etc.)\n- **`runDatabricksPrivateCli`**: Execute private CLI commands (notebook cells, asset search)\n- **`executeCode`**: Run SQL or Python code on compute\n- **`createAsset`**: Create new workspace assets (notebooks, dashboards, pipelines, jobs, queries, files)\n- **`editAsset`**: Edit existing asset content\n- **`openAsset`**: Navigate to an asset's page (with optional `continueMessage` for handoff)\n- **`readAssetById`**: Read an asset's current content before modifying\n- **`searchAssets`** / **`forYouAssets`**: Find relevant workspace assets\n- **`readTable`** / **`tableSearch`**: Explore table schemas and metadata\n- **`docSearch`**: Search Databricks documentation\n"}}]);
